 with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"title":"Interaction_DragView"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)-8zo3w":{"title":"accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/accessibilityrotor(_:textranges:)-8zo3w","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accessibilityRotor"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AccessibilitySystemRotor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI24AccessibilitySystemRotorV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"textRanges"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Range","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sn"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS5IndexV"},{"kind":"text","text":">]) -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP"}],"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)-8zo3w","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}]}}}